{
  "title": "Label-line heads start with EVA o at least twice as often as paragraph-line heads",
  "statement": "Among certain first words of IVTFF label and paragraph lines, the rate whose first EVA-basic glyph is o is at least twice as high for labels. The one-sided ratio exceeds the within-page label reassignment null at p at most 0.01 over 399 permutations.",
  "source": "Voynich Statistical Tests, chapter 17, 'Label words have a different shape' (https://projectzero1.xsrv.jp/report.html). The prior work compares all words of label lines with running words by position. This file gives the symmetric first-word statistic and a same-page null.",
  "spec": {
    "select": {
      "certain": true
    },
    "statistic": {
      "ratio": {
        "feature": {
          "prefix": 1
        },
        "in": [
          "o"
        ],
        "of": {
          "unit": [
            "L"
          ],
          "position": "line_initial"
        },
        "to": {
          "unit": [
            "P"
          ],
          "position": "line_initial"
        }
      }
    },
    "compare": [
      {
        "op": ">=",
        "value": 2.0
      },
      {
        "null": "shuffle_labels_within_page",
        "perms": 399,
        "p": 0.01,
        "direction": "greater"
      }
    ]
  },
  "practice_evidence": {
    "normalization": "Only certain first words count. A later word does not replace an excluded uncertain lead. The observed comparison uses line-initial tokens on both sides.",
    "null_scope": "The scored DSL comparison reallocates label positions using words available on their pages. Its eligible shuffle pool covers positions beyond line starts.",
    "strict_public_sensitivities": "The separate conditional exact calculation matches both the page and the line-initial position. The length check also matches the EVA-basic word length and retains only observed mixed cells. These are sensitivity checks on published practice partitions.",
    "formal_spec_sha256": "6e102f9950ae1c32d491b6564a5112e8f6d6b34731273aababb6f98a5220ba4e",
